Subject: registrations swept after a module goes; C3-1 section 4 refusals

From the stage-3 audit (amix-dlm docs/plan/stage-3-audit-2026-10-26.md
section 1.3, 1.5).  A failed _load that attached, or an _unload that
forgot, left an interrupt-chain entry, an ifstats link or the console
hook pointing into freed memory.  The core now sweeps them after every
_unload and after a failed _load, and names what it removed (plan patch
14, "every registration tracked").  C3-1 section 4: a section type
outside the list and an image over the limit are ENOLOAD (were ERELOC,
ENOMEM); each refusal prints one line naming the module and the rule;
parameter defaults are checked against C3-1 section 3's value forms;
word 0 of .moddata must be one R_68K_32 with addend 0.  New harness and
error-path cases.

